  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PRCS/L Conflict Response Plan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since October 2023, the conflict between Hamas and Israel has escalated, leading to immense humanitarian needs in the Gaza Strip and the West Bank. The hostilities have also affected security and socio-economic stability in neighboring countries including Lebanon, especially in southern Lebanon and the Bekaa region. Rockets, bombs, crossfire and hostilities have caused deaths, injuries, displacement, loss of livelihoods and socio-economic insecurity to people living in conflict zones. This necessitates response measures from Palestinian Red Crescent Society &#x2013; Lebanon branch (PRCS-L), Lebanese Red Cross and other humanitarian entities to ensure the health and wellbeing of all people affected by the conflict.

Since October 2023, PRCS-L has taken proactive measures to enhance conflict response . This includes establishing comprehensive contingency plans, conducting refresher courses for first responders and providing first aid training for the volunteers as well as psychological first aid training for the nurses working at the hospitals. The resilience demonstrated by PRCS-L in delivering life-saving services during both peaceful periods and times of conflict underscores the organization&apos;s commitment to serving vulnerable communities under any circumstances.

Despite this generous support from partners, the PRCS-L branch is facing significant financial challenges to respond to the current needs and to preposition items in preparation of a further escalation of the conflict.  The socio-economic crisis in Lebanon and the increased number of patients using PRCS-L facilities has led to a deficit in the availability of medicine and medical supplies. As a result, some hospitals under PRCS/L have been forced to utilize their prepositioned stock to meet the growing demand for healthcare services, thereby limiting the ability of PRCS-L to respond to any further escalation of the conflict.</narrative>
  </description>
